{"chunk_id": "81428d093a37", "text": "The sage Vishwamitra responds to King Dasaratha\u2019s courteous welcome by revealing the true reason for his visit. While performing sacred sacrifices meant to increase his spiritual power, he is repeatedly attacked by two powerful rakshasas, Maricha and Suvahu, who defile the ritual with blood and flesh just as it nears completion. Because the vows of sacrifice forbid him from giving way to anger or cursing them, Vishwamitra cannot retaliate. Instead, he asks Dasaratha to send the young prince Rama with him for ten days so the boy may guard the rite and destroy the demons. Vishwamitra promises protection, divine instruction, and future glory for Rama. The request marks a crucial turning point: it is the moment when Rama first leaves the royal court and begins the heroic, world-shaping deeds that will reveal his divine destiny.\nSage Vishwamitra asks King Dasaratha to send Rama with him to protect a sacrifice from the demons Maricha and Subahu.\nThemes: sage\u2013king relationship, duty over parental attachment, protection of sacrifice, emergence of Rama's heroism", "vector": [0.012133952230215073, -0.041963253170251846, -0.003622224321588874, -0.004729846492409706, -0.012014209292829037, 0.036987267434597015, -0.027407830581068993, -0.025744734331965446, -0.0208352729678154, -0.011714852415025234, 0.014236106537282467, 0.008362049236893654, 0.008787802420556545, -0.0009529543458484113, -0.003984779119491577, 0.007896382361650467, 0.05619935691356659, -0.02396189421415329, 0.017269594594836235, 0.0026859010104089975, 0.003758598119020462, -0.01725628972053528, 0.00659916689619422, 0.023975199088454247, -0.01210734248161316, 0.005019225180149078, 0.010956480167806149, -0.016564441844820976, -0.004204308148473501, -0.024148162454366684, -0.009253469295799732, -0.022671332582831383, 0.005850773770362139, -0.01683053746819496, -0.030068784952163696, -0.0014527147868648171, 0.0030617606826126575, -0.005451630335301161, 0.01696358434